          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+physics"} quantum physics
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            %em fermions
            ares
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/particles"} particles
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+fields"} quantum fields
            with fermionic
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/particle+statistics"} particle statistics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wavefunctions"} wavefunctions
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+many-body+physics"} several
            such particles is
            %em skew-symmetric
            under the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutation"} permutation
            of their parameters (positions), cf. the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pauli+exclusion+principle"} Pauli exclusion principle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bosons"} bosons
            for which the wavefunction is symmetric.
          %p
            By the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin-statistics+theorem"} spin-statistics theorem
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin"} spin
            is half an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integer"} integer
            but not itself an integer.
          %p
            In the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+particle+physics"} standard model of particle physics
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+cosmology"} standard model of cosmology
            fermions are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matter"} matter
            constituents of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/observable+universe"} observable universe
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bosons"} bosons
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quanta"} quanta
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/force"} force
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+fields"} gauge fields
          %p
            The formalization of fermions is in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} supergeometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sections"} sections
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinor+bundles"} spinor bundles
            with odd-degree fibers in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} supergeometry
            %em
              %span.newWikiWord
                Fermi-Dirac statistics
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Fermi-Dirac+statistics"} ?
            and the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pauli+exclusion+principle"} Pauli exclusion principle
